---
// Prerendered at build time so the same page is served from S3/CloudFront and the container.
export const prerender = true;

import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Pianoforte"
	description="What this site is, who writes it, and how it is built."
	pubDate={new Date('October 19 2026')}
>
	<p>
		<strong>Pianoforte</strong> is a journey through classical piano music, from Johann Sebastian Bach to the
		living virtuoso Marc-André Hamelin. Each composer has a profile, a short demo played on the visual piano,
		and a colour theme you can apply to the whole site. The <strong>Scriabin</strong> theme uses the colours
		Alexander Scriabin associated with each musical key, which is where this site began: as a Scriabin piano
		journal.
	</p>

	<h2>About the demos</h2>
	<p>
		The Bach and Mozart demos are the exact opening bars of the Prelude in C major, BWV 846, and the Sonata in
		C major, K. 545. The Scriabin demo is his Mystic chord and Prometheus scale. The other demos are original
		sketches written for this site in each composer's style; they are clearly labelled and are not quotations.
		Marc-André Hamelin's compositions are under copyright and are not reproduced here.
	</p>

	<h2>How it is built</h2>
	<p>
		The site is an <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> project built for the CS4421 DevOps module at the
		University of Limerick. The static pages are served from Amazon S3 through CloudFront, and the dynamic
		version runs as a Docker container on AWS with a <code>/api/health</code> probe. Every change goes through
		a pull request with linting, type checks, unit, integration and end-to-end tests. The piano uses the Web
		Audio API: every note is synthesised in your browser.
	</p>
</Layout>
